        "original_id": "bfcebfe7-4c10-5a9f-82e9-dfb3c2905866",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: qutebrowser, DuckDuckGo\n- Systems: Linux, Windows, macOS\n- Concepts: vim-style key bindings, minimal GUI, default search engine, search result sources\n\nFacts:\n- qutebrowser is a web browser for Linux, Windows, and macOS.\n- qutebrowser has vim-style key bindings and a minimal GUI.\n- qutebrowser uses DuckDuckGo as its default search engine.\n- DuckDuckGo emphasizes returning the best results rather than the most results.\n- DuckDuckGo generates search results from more than 400 sources, including Wikipedia, Bing, Yahoo!, Yandex, and Yummly.",
